:: Day2Start [nobr]
<div class="title-screen">
<div class="th">दूसरा दिन</div>
<div class="te">Day 2   "Saazish" · Conspiracy</div>

<p class="lede">Day 1 is closed. The tracker is clear.</p>

<p class="lede">It's a Saturday morning in Katraj. Arjun brushes his teeth on autopilot, seven hundred consecutive mornings deep, and does not yet know that in a few minutes an unknown number will call and end six months of silence.</p>

<p class="lede">Twenty minutes away, Priya is about to leave Room 304 for a biochemistry lecture, and Meera is about to lock the door and lay out a plan that involves a fourteenth-century manuscript and two people trading bodies at dawn.</p>

<div class="start-btn">
<<link "Wake up   Arjun's morning">><<goto "Hub">><</link>>
</div>
</div>


:: EV_a2_unknown_call
<<img "arjun_call_bathroom.png" "The bathroom call">>
<<run setup.flag("arjun_morning_d2")>>
You're at the sink, toothbrush in your mouth, foam on your chin, when the phone buzzes on the shelf. Unknown number. 8:00 AM.

Your thumb hovers over the red button. Insurance scams, political robocalls, the gym guy who won't stop with the 6 AM motivational forwards. None of it deserves your attention this early.

<div class="choices">
<div class="q">The phone is still buzzing</div>
<<link "Swipe green.">><<goto "EV_a2_unknown_call_answer">><</link>>
<<link "Let it ring out.">><<goto "EV_a2_unknown_call_ring">><</link>>
</div>


:: EV_a2_unknown_call_ring
It stops. Ten seconds of silence. Then it buzzes again — same number. Some vertebra-level instinct makes your thumb move.

<div class="choices">
<<link "Answer">><<goto "EV_a2_unknown_call_answer">><</link>>
</div>


:: EV_a2_unknown_call_answer
<div class="dialogue">"Arjun, yeh Kavya hai. Meera ki roommate. Room 304."<span class="gloss-en">Arjun, this is Kavya. Meera's roommate. Room 304.</span></div>

The toothbrush drops from your mouth. It hits the steel basin with a clang like a starter pistol. Foam drips down your chin onto your bare chest. You don't wipe it.

"Kavya? How   how did you get my number?"

<div class="dialogue">"Meera memorised it. Don't talk, just listen   we don't have long before Priya's back."</div>

A shuffle on the line. A held breath. Then a second voice, low, careful, six months out of reach:

<div class="dialogue">"Arjun." Just your name. Meera's mouth around it. "There might be a way. To see each other. To be   together. Kavya found something."</div>

Your heart doesn't beat   it detonates. Blood rushes to your head so fast your vision fogs. Your knees go liquid. You sit down, right there on the bathroom floor, tiles cold against the backs of your thighs.

"Kya? Kaise?"<span class="gloss-en">What? How?</span>

<div class="dialogue">Kavya again, clipped: "Not on a phone. And not yet   we're still working out whether it even holds. Give us today. Keep tonight free, after 8:15   we'll call you back and explain all of it."</div>

<div class="dialogue">"And Arjun   tomorrow, 5 AM, Pataleshwar temple. Bring your bike. Tell Rohit nothing. Come with an open mind, because what Kavya's going to describe tonight is going to sound completely insane."</div>

Meera, one more time, almost too quiet to catch: //"Bas kal tak."// Just until tomorrow.

Click. Call duration: 2:11. The time it took to tear open the sealed envelope of your life and let light flood in.

Six months. A way. Tonight, after 8:15. Tomorrow, 5 AM.

<<run setup.flag("arjun_received_call")>>
<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_kavya", 4, "arjun")>>
<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_meera", 3, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_pooja_whatsapp
<div class="alert-popup objective" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">💬 Pooja Pagal 🙄</div>

<div class="chat-log">
<div class="msg them">Bhaiya tu aaj subah phone pe kuch alag lag raha tha<span class="gloss-en">Brother, you sounded different on the phone this morning</span></div>
<div class="msg them">Like happy but also terrified??</div>
<div class="msg them">Maine Aai ko bola, she said "woh pagal hai." But Aai doesn't know everything<span class="gloss-en">I told Ma, she said "he's crazy."</span></div>
<div class="msg them">Also maths doubt   quadratic formula. x = -b ± √(b²-4ac) / 2a. Right?? Or did I mess up the signs again</div>
</div>

You reply that the formula's right, the signs are right, and you're fine   just didn't sleep. She fires back: //your typing speed increased which means you're nervous. I AM A DETECTIVE.// Then: //whatever it is, be careful. I don't want Colonel uncle to yell at you.//

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_sunset_energy
Five-thirty. The light goes the colour of weak chai. The restlessness that's been building all day crests   you need to //move,// to //do,// to //prepare.// Set the alarm. Choose the shirt. Scout the temple. Anything but sit still with the size of tomorrow.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_aai_call
<div class="alert-popup swap" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">📞 Aai ❤️</div>

<div class="dialogue">"Beta, Sunday confirm hai na? Mutton already le liya. 350 rupay ka. Wapas nahi jaata."<span class="gloss-en">Son, Sunday's confirmed, right? Already bought the mutton. 350 rupees' worth. It doesn't go back.</span></div>

"Aai, kal subah kuch important hai "<span class="gloss-en">Ma, something important is happening tomorrow morning </span>

<div class="dialogue">"Sunday ko kal subah nahi hai. Sunday ko Sunday hai. 11 baje aa. Sheera bana rahi hoon. Pooja ne kaha tu khush lag raha hai   sach hai?"<span class="gloss-en">Sunday morning isn't tomorrow morning. Come at 11. I'm making sheera. Pooja says you seem happy   is it true?</span></div>

The question sits between you. Your mother — a woman who teaches Class 4 Marathi and possesses the emotional radar of a Soviet-era early-warning system.

<div class="choices">
<div class="q">What do you tell her?</div>
<<link "\"Haan, Aai. Thoda better.\" — Yes, Ma. A little better.">>
	<<run setup.flag("sunday_decision_made")>>
	<<goto "EV_a2_aai_call_yes">>
<</link>>
<<link "\"Aai, main Sunday nahi aa paunga.\" — Ma, I can't make Sunday.">>
	<<run setup.flag("sunday_decision_made")>>
	<<goto "EV_a2_aai_call_no">>
<</link>>
</div>


:: EV_a2_aai_call_yes
Silence. The kind that means she's crying — not sad, the silent grateful crying of a mother who watched her son dissolve for six months and just heard //thoda better.//

<div class="dialogue">"Aa Sunday ko. Bahut pyaar karta hoon, beta."<span class="gloss-en">Come Sunday. I love you so much, son.</span></div>

"Main bhi, Aai."

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_aai_call_no
A long pause. <div class="dialogue">"Theek hai, beta. Mutton fridge mein rakh dungi. Jab aa sake, aa jaana."<span class="gloss-en">Alright, son. I'll put the mutton in the fridge. Come whenever you can.</span></div>

She doesn't push. Which is somehow worse than if she did.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_callback
<<img "arjun_anticipation_night.png" "PG room, 9:14 PM">>
Rohit's at the gym   leg day, back no earlier than 10:30. The unknown number lights up again at 9:14, exactly as promised.

You don't remember picking up. Eleven minutes. Kavya does most of it, in the flat clean voice of someone reading out a lab protocol: a fourteenth-century palm-leaf manuscript, a Sanskrit ritual, a test she ran with Meera last night   ninety seconds in each other's bodies. //Deha-vinimaya.// Body exchange. She says it's real the way you'd say water is wet.

Then the part that stops your breathing: tomorrow it's you and her. You go into the hostel in Kavya's body. She rides your Pulsar to VIT. Meera gets the boyfriend the Colonel took from her. You get   a woman's body for a day, and Meera at the end of it.

"Deal," you hear yourself say, before your brain has finished objecting.

<div class="dialogue">"There are rules   Meera helped write them, you'll get them tomorrow. 5 AM. Pataleshwar. Don't be late, and don't sleep too well. Nothing about tomorrow will feel the way tired feels tonight."</div>

Click. You sit on the floor with your back against the cot, phone still warm in your hand, and try to hold a plan that shouldn't be physically possible. By sunrise you will not be in this body.

<<run setup.flag("arjun_briefed")>>
<<run setup.flag("full_briefing_done")>>
<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_kavya", 5, "arjun")>>
<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_meera", 2, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_priya_class
Priya scoops up her bag at 6:50. "Kavya, Pathak sir ka lecture. Tu aa rahi hai?"<span class="gloss-en">Pathak sir's lecture. You coming?</span> You mumble something about catching up. The door closes. Footsteps recede. Meera's hand is already on the bolt.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_papa_whatsapp
<div class="alert-popup danger" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">💬 Papa</div>

<div class="chat-log">
<div class="msg them">Pharmacology III exam date: October 15. Prepare well.</div>
<div class="msg them">Send your last three internal assessment marks.</div>
<div class="msg them">Sunday lunch. Vaishali. Bring the marks.</div>
</div>

Three messages, zero questions about how you are. You lock the Samsung. The Redmi in your other pocket holds the life you actually live.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_github_issue
<div class="alert-popup objective" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">🔔 GitHub   issue assigned</div>

On the Redmi: //Issue #89   Hindi compound-word tokenization fails on Sanskrit loanwords. Assigned to KV_Codes.// Your specialty. And a Telegram from Rahul: //the maintainer DM'd me asking for your real name. 3 years and I still don't know if you're a dude, a lady, or a very smart crow.//

Tomorrow, in Arjun's body, you could join a video call. Show a face. A male voice, male hands, and nobody would question KV_Codes. The irony is layered enough to be a thesis.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_meera_reminder
Meera passes you in the corridor and doesn't slow down. Sideways, barely moving her lips:

<div class="dialogue">"Call him tonight. After Priya leaves for the common room. Everything depends on it."</div>

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_priya_gossip
Priya bursts back from her jog sweating and vibrating with narrative. Something about Room 308, Anjali, a boyfriend, and a window. She's dying to tell you the whole thing   go find her in the room.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a2_priya_common
8:15. Priya grabs a packet of chips and heads for the common room   //Sasural Simar Ka// rerun. "Kavya aa na!" You wave her off. The door closes. Meera looks at you. It's time to call him.

<<hubreturn>>


